.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PCAPSH_PROTOS_DIR
Directory of
.B .posa
files to load at startup instead of the installed one.
.TP
.B SSLKEYLOGFILE
NSS key log loaded automatically for TLS decryption in
.BR rdpcap() .
.TP
.B HOME
Location of
.IR ~/.pcapsh_protos.posa .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/pcapsh/protos/*.posa
Bundled protocol definitions (under the installation prefix).
.TP
.I ~/.pcapsh_protos.posa
Personal protocol definitions, loaded every time.
Created with TFTP and Telnet examples on first run if missing.
.TP
.I ./.pcapsh_history
Interactive history, kept in the current directory.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
.B wrpcap()
never truncates; remove the output file to start over.
.IP \(bu 2
Loop counters start at 1 with
.BI range( n ) ;
use an offset such as
.B sport=49000+$i
to stay out of well\-known ports.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ether()
defaults to the IPv4 ethertype; ARP frames need
.BR type=0x0806 .
.IP \(bu 2
Some posa layers model only a fixed header (for example SMB2 without a
command body, or KRB5's 18\-byte DER prefix); Wireshark may flag such packets
as malformed.
Append the body as a string payload when you need a clean dissection.
.IP \(bu 2
Output is coloured with ANSI escapes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tshark (1),
.BR wireshark (1),
.BR tcpdump (1),
